#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562428 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90455606-1080-552e-a825-0cc7054b4be3" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Fractions in One Equation Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98f282bc-fb6e-570b-ac24-148369f2484f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98f282bc-fb6e-570b-ac24-148369f2484f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561961} :answer-field/id #uuid "76226d76-f5d2-55d4-8a7f-5814323e67f0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562298} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a7bd31c-5ecb-5b23-90cc-98381162c779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a7bd31c-5ecb-5b23-90cc-98381162c779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561773} :answer-field/id #uuid "80927105-5be2-594a-95d0-2c7fe3bfa8ca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562305}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "40e64447-ceb6-5045-8392-d608f9b3b14b" :question/math-academy-id "q-208827" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y=7 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{3}+4y=-\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions in the second equation, we must multiply the second equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $3.$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y=7 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{3}+4y=-\\frac{8}{3} & |\\,\\times 3\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y=7 \\\\ 2x+12y=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Let's solve for $x$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-5y & =7 \\\\ x & =5y+7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute $x=5y+7$ into the second equation and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+12y & =-8 \\\\ 2(5y+7)+12y & =-8 \\\\ 10y+14+12y & =-8 \\\\ 22y+14 & =-8 \\\\ 22y & =-22 \\\\ y & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $x,$ we substitute $y=-1$ into the equation $x=5y+7,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5y+7 \\\\  & =5(-1)+7 \\\\  & =-5+7 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=2,\\,y=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562476 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096635 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7eb3fea-e4cf-5537-9a33-06b9d2b35c6b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Fractions in Both Equations Using Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6ab6e7a-d92d-5ecf-8a85-faffe97c6157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6ab6e7a-d92d-5ecf-8a85-faffe97c6157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562118} :answer-field/id #uuid "08b0a80b-6e11-58dd-a2f8-eea08773e1f7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562224} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "954a215e-6bc2-56e2-86bb-f73d149f278b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "954a215e-6bc2-56e2-86bb-f73d149f278b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561952} :answer-field/id #uuid "28c5e5b8-30fa-5781-8559-a9e4f5d972ae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562246}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b1b90563-ce29-5141-8ac6-0ac20bb77c12" :question/math-academy-id "q-216312" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{4}p+3q=25 \\\\ p+\\frac{2}{5}q=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,q=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $4$ and the second equation by $5,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{4}p+3q=25 & |\\times 4 \\\\ p+\\frac{2}{5}q=0 & |\\times 5\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}5p+12q=100 \\\\ 5p+2q=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-1,$ then we will get a $-5p$ term that can cancel with the $5p$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5p+12q=100 & |\\,\\times (-1) \\\\ 5p+2q=0 & \\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-5p-12q=-100 \\\\ 5p+2q=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $p$-variable, and allows us to solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{-5p}-12q & =-100 \\\\ \\cancel{5p}+2q & =0 \\\\ (-12q+2q) & =(-100+0) \\\\ -10q & =-100 \\\\ q & =\\frac{100}{10} \\\\ q & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $q=10$ into the second equation to solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5p+2q & =0 \\\\ 5p+2\\cdot 10 & =0 \\\\ 5p+20 & =0 \\\\ 5p & =-20 \\\\ p & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system is $p=-4,\\,q=10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562508 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90455606-1080-552e-a825-0cc7054b4be3" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Fractions in One Equation Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f67813b-4012-57a6-aa60-6e1f4b03c49b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-4,\\,b=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561706} {:answer/id #uuid "4931d63f-6063-5b84-9f38-d5b26851222a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-2,\\,b=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561767} {:answer/id #uuid "8ac277a4-9539-5e8e-a05e-de4f499992b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561929} {:answer/id #uuid "b09fc133-c399-5f21-8549-810bcfd05f1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562020} {:answer/id #uuid "e66e2e44-a83a-5b53-8541-fd9e66215cf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=2,\\,b=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f67813b-4012-57a6-aa60-6e1f4b03c49b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-4,\\,b=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561706} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e76924e-7974-5bfd-a8ee-f608b55003f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562272}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ef9f41c7-171c-5068-8a8d-ff2c5135b2da" :question/math-academy-id "q-26475" :question/problem "Find the solution to the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2a+3b=-2 \\\\ \\frac{a}{3}-\\frac{b}{6}=-\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the fractions in the second equation, we must multiply the second equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $6.$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2a+3b=-2 \\\\ \\frac{a}{3}-\\frac{b}{6}=-\\frac{5}{3} & |\\,\\times 6\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}2a+3b=-2 \\\\ 2a-b=-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Let's solve for $b$ in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a-b & =-10 \\\\ b & =2a+10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute $b=2a+10$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+3b & =-2 \\\\ 2a+3(2a+10) & =-2 \\\\ 2a+6a+30 & =-2 \\\\ 8a & =-32 \\\\ a & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $b,$ we substitute $a=-4$ into the equation $b=2a+10$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =2a+10 \\\\  & =2(-4)+10 \\\\  & =-8+10 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-4,\\,b=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562489 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096635 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7eb3fea-e4cf-5537-9a33-06b9d2b35c6b" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Fractions in Both Equations Using Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0699480b-fcdd-5aa7-bd88-db69b130f0d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-16,\\,y=-63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561602} {:answer/id #uuid "6bef9576-7456-5c97-8c11-0c2e8958fa4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-12,\\,y=-48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561851} {:answer/id #uuid "8db89ec1-822e-58c5-b2f7-ab0ed448f0e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=16,\\,y=32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561936} {:answer/id #uuid "b57c8f87-09f5-526e-925b-2fa685384d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-32,\\,y=-26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562033} {:answer/id #uuid "cbca4dac-d673-5f55-816e-2823843ec578" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-63,\\,y=-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0699480b-fcdd-5aa7-bd88-db69b130f0d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-16,\\,y=-63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561602} :answer-field/id #uuid "61aac299-670f-5a9c-bbec-1956ec185e42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562281}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "be4c74c9-6e39-5f39-a1ce-fbc98923b17f" :question/math-academy-id "q-52203" :question/problem "Find the solution to the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-\\frac{2}{7}y=2 \\\\ -x+\\frac{2}{9}y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $7$ and the second equation by $9,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-\\frac{2}{7}y=2 & |\\times 7 \\\\ -x+\\frac{2}{9}y=2 & |\\times 9\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}7x-2y=14 \\\\ -9x+2y=18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. We can eliminate $y$ by adding the two equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x-\\cancel{2y} & =14 \\\\ -9x+\\cancel{2y} & =18 \\\\ (7x-9x) & =(14+18) \\\\ -2x & =32 \\\\ x & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x=-16$ into the first equation to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x-2y & =14 \\\\ 7(-16)-2y & =14 \\\\ -112-2y & =14 \\\\ -2y & =126 \\\\ y & =-63\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system is $x=-16$ and $y=-63.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562491 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096637 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2c880ac-41a9-543f-b7a1-b4dfcc5de99d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Fractions in Both Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e086611-7bec-50f9-b80f-9f7d167a7576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3,\\,y=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561855} {:answer/id #uuid "8ca432f5-bc7b-5a9d-8960-0c52d5ad9bb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=8,\\,y=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561933} {:answer/id #uuid "b01ccc0c-d6e0-5c8b-8e5f-f9b6e7de0c3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4,\\,y=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562018} {:answer/id #uuid "b92976d9-53dd-5053-b478-c050ea85c203" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-6,\\,y=-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562052} {:answer/id #uuid "cd47a55d-6fb7-5018-956e-7585cfc1af31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3,\\,y=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b92976d9-53dd-5053-b478-c050ea85c203" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-6,\\,y=-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562052} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1e0f312-cd0e-5c8b-a953-be01ee2625b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c2c2c978-aae7-58d4-874a-c874d05efc9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-75861" :question/problem "Find the solution to the  following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}y=-1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{1}{2}y=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $4$ and the second equation by $6,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}y=-1 & |\\times 4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{1}{2}y=-6 & |\\times 6\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=-4 \\\\ 2x+3y=-36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-1,$ then we will get a $-2x$ term that can cancel with the $2x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=-4 & |\\,\\times (-1) \\\\ 2x+3y=-36 & \\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+y=4 \\\\ 2x+3y=-36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $x$-variable, and allows us to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{-2x}+y & =4 \\\\ \\cancel{2x}+3y & =-36 \\\\ (y+3y) & =(4-36) \\\\ 4y & =-32 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{32}{4} \\\\ y & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=-8$ into the first equation to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-y & =-4 \\\\ 2x-(-8) & =-4 \\\\ 2x+8 & =-4 \\\\ 2x & =-12 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{12}{2} \\\\ x & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system is $x=-6,\\,y=-8.$"}]}
